      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To make this recipe more detailed and comprehensive, I've added a bit more information to each step while maintaining a natural flow. Here's the revised version:\n\n\"Begin by heating a pan over medium heat and adding a pat of butter. Once the butter has melted, sauté the chopped onions until they're softened and translucent, stirring occasionally to prevent burning. This should take about 5-7 minutes, or until the onions have lost their raw smell and are lightly golden. Next, add the minced garlic and stir to combine, allowing it to cook for about 1 minute, until fragrant. Then, pour in the heavy cream and season with salt and pepper to taste, whisking gently to prevent lumps. Finally, add a handful of fresh spinach leaves and let them wilt into the sauce, stirring occasionally, until they're fully incorporated and the sauce has thickened slightly. Serve the creamy spinach sauce over cooked pasta and enjoy!\"\n\nThis revised version provides more detail in each step, while still maintaining a clear and readable format. The added information should help meet the thoroughness check requirements for the premium edition.",
